<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">K'inich Yax K'uk' Mo'</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 426–437</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">K'inich Yax K'uk' Mo' was the founder of the royal dynasty of Copán, in present-day Honduras, who took power in 426 CE. Inscriptions link him to Teotihuacan and Tikal, and a tomb believed to be his lies deep beneath the Acropolis. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jacobite-rising-of-1715">Fifteen</a> later kings traced their descent from him, and his agents refounded Quiriguá as a dependency of Copán.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kinich-yax-kuk-mo.jpg" alt="K'inich Yax K'uk' Mo'" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: DuendeThumb · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yax_Kuk_Mo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
